{"questions":[{"question_id":"OF4fQ69S9QNL7Qbo","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2013 (Offline)","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"alcohols-phenols-and-ethers","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"properties-preparation-and-uses-of-alcohols","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"an-unknown-alcohol-is-treated-with-the-lucas-reagent-t-2013-marks-4-of4fq69s9qnl7qbo.htm","content":"An unknown alcohol is treated with the “Lucas reagent” to determine whether the alcohol is primary,\nsecondary or tertiary. Which alcohol reacts fastest and by what mechanism: ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"tertiary alcohol by S<sub>N</sub>1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"secondary alcohol by S<sub>N</sub>2"},{"identifier":"C","content":"tertiary alcohol by S<sub>N</sub>2"},{"identifier":"D","content":"secondary alcohol by S<sub>N</sub>1 "}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"Tertiary alcohols reacts fastest with lucas reagnet as the rate of reaction is directly proportional to the stability of carbocation formed in the reaction. Since most stable <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.119ex\" height=\"1.581ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 936.6 699\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(533,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> carbocation is formed in the reaction hence it will react fastest further tetriary alcohols appears to react by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.126ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1823.9 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D446\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D446\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(646,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1323.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> mechanism.\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/fHWuWONlEt2DaP0iH/rOSfnYYSzLV5kF24XQNhyOEHgHUu3/OZ7xqcfqGGcpzZfrhBkSmO/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2013 (Offline) Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 172 English Explanation\"> "}]}